[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is Key Light Air Mark II. A soft, professional light in a 15-in panel that fits on any desk, powered via a single USB cable, control it your way over Wi-Fi, USB, Stream Deck, or a tap on the panel, and move it wherever the'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shot takes you with MagSafe mounting. It\'s the most versatile light we\'ve ever made. But, to see why a light like this matters so much, forget the camera for a second. When you\'re recording a video, it\'s not the camera that makes you look'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'good. It\'s your lighting. You can own the most expensive camera on the market, but in a dim room, it\'s got nothing to work with. The result will be grainy, flat, without depth. Give that camera, or even a basic'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'webcam, good light, and it\'ll transform how you look. So, let\'s talk about light and how Key Light Air Mark II is built to deliver it, starting with where it comes from, a 15-in edge-lit LED panel. Instead of firing 256 LEDs straight at'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you, the light comes from the edges, reflects off the back, and passes through diffusion, spreading into one smooth, even glow across the whole surface. There\'s no hot spots and no hard, unflattering shadows on your face,'

[01:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just soft, diffused light that looks natural on camera and stays easy on your eyes throughout long sessions. At full power, Key Light Air Mark II reaches up to 2,100 lm. That\'s more light than most people have hanging from'

[01:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'their ceiling. This ensures there\'s more than enough light for even the darkest rooms. And because it renders color with over 94% CRI accuracy, skin tones, backgrounds, and everything in frame'

[01:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stay true to life. Have you ever considered what white light actually looks like? A candle glows warm and orange, midday sun is cool and blue. That\'s color temperature, measured in Kelvin, and Key Light Air Mark II'

[01:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'supports a wide range, from a cozy 2,900 up to a crisp, cool 7,000. So, why adjust it? Well, because different shots need different light. Warm it up for a relaxed flattering look when you\'re'

[02:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'talking to camera. Cool it toward daylight when you\'re shooting a product unboxing where the colors have to stay true to life. Key Light Air Mark II is powered via USB-C. It\'s just one cable and how you provide that power is up to you. You can plug it'

[02:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'straight into your computer and you\'ve got enough soft light for most creator setups. No wall adapter needed. A typical USB-C port offers up to 15 W which gives you around 750 lm. Plenty for talking to the camera. If you want'

[02:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the full 2,100 lm, connect a USB-C PD power adapter like the Elgato P30 power adapter or a compatible power bank rated at 30 W or higher and the panel scales all the way up. So, you have a choice of'

[02:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'how to power it. Your computer, wall adapter, or battery, all with a single cable. Mounting Key Light Air Mark II is fast and convenient with the included stand. It clamps to the edge of your desk,'

[02:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'saving the space a tripod would take. The ball mount lets you tilt and rotate to the exact angle you want and the height markings help you land the same position every time when making adjustments or using two lights at the same time. On the back of Key Light Air'

[03:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Mark II, you\'ll find three industry standard quarter-inch threaded mount points, so you can mount the light horizontal or vertical. Brand new is the inclusion of MagSafe. Key Light Air Mark II can snap onto any MagSafe compatible'

[03:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mount. This makes it incredibly easy to move from an overhead light for an unboxing to a face level key light for talking to the camera. Just pop it off one mount and snap it onto the next. It\'s like the ultimate quick connect'

[03:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'system. MagSafe also means you can attach a MagSafe battery to the back. Mount Key Light Air Mark II, snap on the battery, connect a cable, and you\'ve got a portable light ready at any moment. So, how you mount it is up to you.'

[03:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Vertical, horizontal, with a threaded mount or MagSafe. Now, most of the time, you want soft light that fills the whole scene. But, sometimes you want the opposite. Light that falls exactly where you point it'

[03:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and lets everything else cast a shadow for a moody aesthetic. That\'s done with the optional focus grid. It snaps on magnetically and tightens the wide cone of light into a controlled beam. Instead of covering the whole room, it'

[04:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lands on you and stays there. So, the background falls away and your shot gains depth and contrast. It\'s the difference between well-lit and shot with intent. Moody portraits, dramatic close-ups, a product that comes off screen against a dark background.'

[04:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'With one accessory, the same panel goes from soft and even to sharp and cinematic. The best way to control Key Light Air Mark II is to barely think about it. So, most of the time you won\'t touch the light at all. Thanks to Wi-Fi'

[04:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or the direct USB-C connection, Elgato Control Center puts brightness and color temperature controls right on your computer or on your phone. And because it works with any Stream Deck, your lighting sits right next to your scenes,'

[04:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your mic, and everything else you already run. Just tap a key to turn it on or turn a dial to adjust brightness. And when reaching is the quick way, capacitive touch buttons on the front panel adjust brightness and color temperature or recall two saved'

[05:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'favorites with a single tap. And you\'ll also find a power button at the bottom of the light. Wi-Fi, USB, Stream Deck, or the buttons on the light itself, however you like to work, the control is already there. So,'

[05:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'who is Key Light Air Mark II for? If you\'re a streamer, it keeps you looking good for the whole stream. Flattering light that\'s easy on the eyes and quick to change from your Stream Deck when the scene changes.'

[05:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you\'re an artist, it gives you color you can trust. [music] Mount it above your desk for a clean top-down view and let your work shine. And if your day is back-to-back video calls at the office or working from home, just plug it into your laptop and you\'ll look sharp.'

[05:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That\'s it. Whoever you are, wherever you work, Key Light Air Mark II fits the setup you already have. So, that\'s Key Light Air Mark II. Soft, professional light in a 15-in panel that fits any desk and runs on a single USB-C cable.'

[05:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Control it your way over Wi-Fi, USB, or a tap on the panel. And move it wherever the shot takes you with MagSafe. It\'s the most versatile light we\'ve ever made. Great lighting usually comes with'

[06:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a trade-off. Go small and it\'s fine for a call, but never quite right on camera. Go big and you nail the look, but you\'re paying for eye-searing brightness you\'ll never really need. Keylight Air is built for what most people really need. Proper'

[06:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'camera light in a size that fits right in. It\'s the result of years spent building studio lighting for creators, and it\'s our most versatile light yet. Keylight Air Mark II is available now for $140, and you\'ll find pricing and availability'

[06:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for your region at elgato.com. Thanks for watching.'
